<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n112681" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φῡσ-ητήρ</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῆρος</span>,
			ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>instrument for blowing, blowpipe</i> or <i>tube,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φ. ὀστέϊνοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					4.2
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Opp.
				<u>H.</u>
				4.463
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>bellows,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Jb.</u>
				32.19
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				10.147
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				2.717
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>blow-hole</i> or <i>spiracle</i> of whales, etc., <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				566b3
			</span></i>; the <i>funnel</i> through which the cuttle-fish squirts
			its ink, ib.<i><span class="en">
				541b17
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>one who blows a pipe</i> or <i>bellows,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				5.75
			</span></i> (v.l.), <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i>
			
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐξέλιπε.</span>
			
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> a kind of <i>whale,</i>
			perh. <i>Biscay whale,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Str.
				3.2.7
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
